\b\fs32 FORM 2 \u2014 THE PATENTS ACT, 1970 \u2014 Complete Specification\b0\fs22\par
\b\fs28 TITLE OF THE INVENTION\b0\fs22\par
A BROWSER-NATIVE PRIVACY-PRESERVING SYSTEM AND METHOD FOR HYSTERESIS-FILTERED REAL-TIME YOGA POSE COACHING WITH PRIORITY-RESOLVED VOICE COMMAND GRAMMAR\par\par
\b\fs28 (a) FIELD OF THE INVENTION\b0\fs22\par
The present invention relates to the field of computer-assisted physical instruction, more particularly to systems and methods for real-time pose-correction feedback during yoga practice using on-device machine learning inference and voice-driven hands-free interaction. The invention further relates to multi-tenant architecture for deploying such systems at institutional scale.\par\par
\b\fs28 (b) BACKGROUND OF THE INVENTION\b0\fs22\par
Existing AI-assisted yoga systems suffer from at least the following deficiencies:\par\par
(i) **Native-app distribution dependence.** Conventional yoga apps require installation through Apple App Store, Google Play Store, or proprietary device sideloading, creating administrative overhead for institutional rollout (educational institutions, corporate wellness programmes) and excluding low-end devices that lack the storage to host such applications.\par\par
(ii) **Cloud-side pose inference.** Existing systems that perform pose estimation on a remote server transmit raw video frames or extracted skeletal data over the network. This (a) introduces latency that defeats real-time coaching, (b) requires reliable broadband connectivity inappropriate for users in low-connectivity regions, and (c) creates a privacy liability \u2014 biometric data is regulated under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.\par\par
(iii) **Frame-level feedback chatter.** Conventional rule-based pose scoring emits an audio correction whenever a rule fails on the current frame and rescinds it whenever the rule passes, producing oscillating spoken feedback (e.g., "lift your knee" and "knee corrected" repeating several times per second) that is cognitively burdensome and counter-productive to practice.\par\par
(iv) **Voice-command ambiguity.** Existing voice-controlled fitness applications cannot distinguish between *action commands* (e.g., "next pose", "what is my score?") and *content references* (e.g., "warrior two" \u2014 referring to the pose Virabhadrasana II). When the spoken token "two" is parsed as a numeral, the action grammar fails, and when the action grammar takes priority, the user cannot verbally select certain poses.\par\par
(v) **Lack of institutional partition.** Existing systems are designed for individual consumers; they do not support a tenant-isolated data model in which a college can onboard 1,000 students with strict guarantees that no other tenant's data is accessible.\par\par
There exists, therefore, a need for a yoga coaching system that (a) runs natively in a browser without app installation, (b) executes pose inference on-device for privacy and latency, (c) suppresses frame-level feedback chatter through stateful filtering, (d) disambiguates voice commands deterministically, and (e) supports multi-tenant institutional deployment.\par\par
The present invention addresses each of the above deficiencies.\par\par
\b\fs28 (c) OBJECTS OF THE INVENTION\b0\fs22\par
The principal objects of the present invention are:\par\par
1. To provide a yoga coaching system that operates in any modern web browser without requiring native application installation.\par
\par
1. To provide such a system in which all biometric inference (pose estimation, alignment scoring) is performed on the user's local computing device and no raw video, image, or skeletal keypoint data is transmitted to any remote server.\par
\par
1. To provide a method of converting per-frame pose rule evaluations into spoken corrections through a per-rule fail/pass debounce filter (hereinafter "hysteresis filter") that suppresses transient detection artefacts and emits feedback only after a sustained condition is observed.\par
\par
1. To provide a voice-command interpretation method that resolves ambiguity between action commands and content references through priority-ordered regular expression matching with a fallback fuzzy pose-name lookup.\par
\par
1. To provide a multi-tenant institutional deployment model in which data is partitioned by organisational email domain with route-level access enforcement.\par
\par
1. To provide a six-semester certificate programme integrating real-time pose evaluation with quiz-based knowledge assessment, issuing cryptographically-signed completion certificates.\par
\par
\b\fs28 (d) SUMMARY OF THE INVENTION\b0\fs22\par
The present invention discloses a system and method for real-time yoga pose coaching, comprising:\par\par
(i) a *client device* (a personal computer, laptop, tablet, or mobile phone) executing a web browser supporting the WebGL and WebSpeech APIs;\par\par
(ii) a *pose estimation module* loaded via the said web browser, comprising a convolutional neural network for single-person pose estimation (in the preferred embodiment, MoveNet SinglePose Thunder) executing within a JavaScript runtime environment using WebGL hardware acceleration;\par\par
(iii) a *rule engine* comprising a finite, per-pose set of predicates over the smoothed keypoints, where each predicate is either an angle constraint between three keypoints or a distance- ratio constraint between two pairs of keypoints, and is associated with a natural-language correction string;\par\par
(iv) a *hysteresis filter* comprising, for each predicate, a fail counter and a pass counter, and a state flag taking values in the set \{silent, speaking\}, wherein: (a) a correction is emitted to a speech synthesis subsystem only when the fail counter for the corresponding rule equals or exceeds a fail threshold (default seven frames); (b) the state flag transitions from speaking back to silent only when the pass counter equals or exceeds a pass threshold (default five frames);\par\par
(v) a *voice command grammar* comprising a priority-ordered list of regular expressions, each mapped to a fixed action handler, with a fallback fuzzy lookup against a catalogue of pose names;\par\par
(vi) a *server-side multi-tenant data layer* in which records are partitioned by an organisational email domain identifier, and read/write operations are gated by a request-level access decorator that injects the requesting user's organisational identifier into the database query;\par\par
(vii) a *certification module* that records per-pose alignment sessions and quiz outcomes, computes per-semester completion, and issues cryptographically signed PDF certificates.\par\par
The said hysteresis filter is the technical heart of the invention; the priority-resolved voice grammar is the second core contribution; the multi-tenant model is the third.\par\par
